exam: It is given that for every {p} red beads upon a string there are {q} blue beads, and that there are {p*m} red beads. Determine the number of blue beads.
exam: Ascertain the number of tulips in a garden wherein the ratio of roses to tulips is {p} to {q} and the roses number {p*m}.
exam: Whereas {q.words} girls are present in a class for every {p.words} boys, and the boys number {p*m}, state the number of girls.
exam: Compute the quantity of the second kind, given a fixed ratio of {p} of the first kind to {q} of the second and a total of {p*m} of the first kind.
exercise: The old hamster was put to sleep, and {a} gets fish for the tank instead: for every {p} goldfish {a.he} buys {q} snails. {a.He} buys {p*m} goldfish. How many snails does {a.he} buy?
exercise: At the "celebration of life" for Grandma, for every {p} sandwiches there were {q} cakes. There were {p*m} sandwiches. How many cakes were there?
test: the shop's "downsizing", means they sacked half of em. for every {p} who stayed, {q} got shown the door. {p*m} stayed. how many got the boot
